# Fullstack Layer Routing

Extension for `@luizsantiago/agentic-fullstack`. Requires Spec-Driven Harness (`agent-architecture.md`).

## Layer registry

Read `.specs/project/PROJECT.md` § **Layer registry** before each Execute task. Each row maps a layer id → skill file → path globs. v1 ships **frontend** and **backend**; future layers (mobile, cli, data, embedded) add a row + install `{layer}-engineering.md` — do not load two layer skills in one turn.

## Execute — which skill to load

| Task `Files` vs registry | Load | Do not load |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Matches **one** layer only | That layer's skill (e.g. `frontend-engineering.md`) | Other layer skills |
| Matches **zero** layers | Neither — follow `engineering-standards.md` only | Layer skills |
| Matches **two or more** layers | **STOP** — split task or amend `tasks.md` | All layer skills |

Always keep `engineering-standards.md` and the current phase reference (`references/implement.md`) in the working set. Layer skills are **additive**, not replacements.

## After commit

Drop the layer skill from context before the next task (same pattern as conditional Verify sisters).

## Verify

Do **not** load layer skills on `/verify`. Use harness Verify stack: `validate.md`, `security-review.md`, then at most one of `appsec.md` or `qa-strategy.md`.

## Re-install safety

Harness `install` overwrites its own skills only. These files are extension-owned: `frontend-engineering.md`, `backend-engineering.md`, this rule. Re-run `npx @luizsantiago/agentic-fullstack install` to refresh the extension.
